   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0f33224b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4.4 Plot ACF and PACF to Choose ARIMA Parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "ARIMA models have three key parameters: p (autoregressive lags), d (number of differences), and q (moving average lags). But how do you pick p and q? The answer: look at the autocorrelation (ACF) and partial autocorrelation (PACF) plots! These plots show how much the current value depends on previous values and help you decide how many lags to include.\n",
    "\n",
    "- ACF: Shows correlation with previous values (lags).\n",
    "- PACF: Shows correlation with previous values, controlling for the values in between.\n",
    "\n",
    "Look for where the plots drop off to zero—this gives you a clue for p and q."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
